WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.139
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:45.713
CHAPTER 4:
STARS ARE BORN OUT OF CHAOS

00:45.796 --> 00:47.256
-Jeon Ji-min.
-Here!

00:48.758 --> 00:50.217
-Oh Ji-ho.
-Here!

00:50.301 --> 00:51.802
-[Woo-su] Kim Ga-yeong.
-Here!

00:51.886 --> 00:53.053
[Eui-ju] He's the new homeroom teacher,

00:53.137 --> 00:55.264
and he's calling roll
before even introducing himself?

00:55.347 --> 00:56.974
-Who does he think he is?
-Kim Dan-ji.

00:57.057 --> 00:58.601
[clears throat] Here!

00:59.477 --> 01:01.061
-Kim Yeong-jae.
-Here!

01:02.021 --> 01:03.564
-Eun Ha-su.
-Here.

01:07.067 --> 01:08.903
You got the Gold Prize in the KMO.

01:10.696 --> 01:12.239
-Yes.
-KMO?

01:12.823 --> 01:14.033
What's that?

01:14.116 --> 01:14.950
Beats me.

01:15.034 --> 01:16.285
How was it?

01:16.869 --> 01:19.371
Hmm. It was not that difficult.

01:19.955 --> 01:22.666
Why does he just say some names,
and only talks to them?

01:23.417 --> 01:24.919
Are they like best friends?

01:25.544 --> 01:26.587
Hmm.

01:26.670 --> 01:27.797
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

01:28.798 --> 01:30.132
-Choi Yu-mi.
-Here.

01:31.258 --> 01:32.468
-Yeo Eui-ju.
-Here.

01:36.889 --> 01:39.058
[whimsical music plays]

01:39.141 --> 01:40.518
-Yeo Eui-ju?
-Here.

01:42.436 --> 01:44.063
-Yeo Eui-ju!
-Here!

01:48.317 --> 01:49.777
[music ends]

01:49.860 --> 01:51.570
-Choi Go-ya.
-Here.

01:51.654 --> 01:53.072
Choi Ji-a.

01:58.160 --> 01:59.578
Choi Ji-a?

01:59.662 --> 02:00.663
Yeah.

02:08.712 --> 02:11.841
I'll be your homeroom teacher as of today,
my name is Ga Woo-su.

02:11.924 --> 02:14.510
[cheering, giggling]

02:15.427 --> 02:17.429
[triumphant music playing]

02:22.476 --> 02:24.645
Math is a discipline with no falsehood.

02:25.354 --> 02:26.814
Euclid's Elements begins with,

02:26.897 --> 02:29.817
"A point is that which has no part…"

02:30.693 --> 02:31.777
Beautiful, isn't it?

02:34.530 --> 02:38.284
Points come together to form lines
which extend to create planes,

02:38.367 --> 02:40.619
planes bound together to build solids.

02:40.703 --> 02:42.538
And solids exist in time and space.

02:42.621 --> 02:43.622
In short,

02:44.540 --> 02:47.001
mathematics is the language that explains

02:47.751 --> 02:49.795
the very existence of the universe.

02:49.879 --> 02:52.590
Thus, learning about the universe
you were born into.

02:54.925 --> 02:55.926
[sighs]

02:57.928 --> 03:00.306
I see all of you as stars in the universe.

03:00.848 --> 03:03.183
Each shining brightly,
with a world of your own.

03:03.267 --> 03:04.435
[students murmuring]

03:05.102 --> 03:06.604
When a star is born,

03:06.687 --> 03:10.065
a massive cloud of dust surrounds it,
blinding everything in sight.

03:10.149 --> 03:11.275
That's why people say,

03:12.359 --> 03:13.777
"stars are born out of chaos."

03:13.861 --> 03:15.863
-Whoa. He's so cool.
-[students gasping]

03:17.239 --> 03:18.449
And so will you be born.

03:18.532 --> 03:20.868
[gasping, sighing] Oh.

03:20.951 --> 03:24.580
What you like, what you hate,
what your talent is, what you truly want…

03:25.080 --> 03:27.416
Some of you may have already found a path
through the chaos.

03:27.499 --> 03:29.209
But if you're not sure yet.

03:29.752 --> 03:31.170
I hope that this year,

03:31.253 --> 03:33.130
will be your time to find those answers.

03:33.213 --> 03:35.215
[students giggling, exclaiming]

03:36.467 --> 03:38.385
I'll be there to help you find your path.

03:41.263 --> 03:42.723
I'll also encourage you

03:43.349 --> 03:45.351
to take the last step on your own.

03:45.434 --> 03:47.853
[students gasping, chattering]

03:47.937 --> 03:49.772
[scoffs] What the heck?

03:49.855 --> 03:52.816
Was all that star and universe talk
just to say that?

03:52.900 --> 03:54.151
Look at that math nerd.

03:54.234 --> 03:55.945
Wow, he's so full of himself.

03:57.154 --> 03:58.155
[Woo-su] Yeo Eui-ju.

03:59.365 --> 04:00.491
Yes.

04:00.574 --> 04:02.993
What was your math score
for the September mock exam?

04:03.786 --> 04:06.038
[Eui-ju] Why is he suddenly asking
about my score?

04:07.081 --> 04:08.248
Uh…

04:08.832 --> 04:10.000
I can't hear you.

04:11.543 --> 04:12.795
[stammers] Four…

04:12.878 --> 04:13.879
Four?

04:15.506 --> 04:17.383
-What did she say?
-Four points.

04:17.466 --> 04:18.884
[giggling]

04:19.635 --> 04:21.053
-[comical music playing]
-That's so bad.

04:21.136 --> 04:23.055
[students murmuring, giggling]

04:23.138 --> 04:25.265
[sighs] Four points, huh?

04:28.352 --> 04:29.561
A four in math…

04:33.065 --> 04:34.066
[thuds]

04:35.192 --> 04:37.403
You might as well start over
from the first grade.

04:37.486 --> 04:39.488
[comical music continues]

04:45.452 --> 04:47.246
Follow me to the teachers' office.

04:48.163 --> 04:49.289
Dismissed.

04:50.416 --> 04:51.417
[gasps]

04:52.584 --> 04:53.669
[sighs]

04:55.963 --> 04:58.424
EPISODE 2

05:17.985 --> 05:18.986
Sir.

05:20.529 --> 05:24.199
I swear.
I didn't take any videos of you. Look.

05:24.908 --> 05:25.743
PHOTO GALLERY

05:25.826 --> 05:26.744
Here.

05:26.827 --> 05:28.996
This is… This the Video folder.

05:29.079 --> 05:31.749
And look. At the Recently Deleted folder.

05:31.832 --> 05:32.833
See? There's nothing.

05:34.501 --> 05:35.335
Right?

05:35.419 --> 05:37.296
[suspenseful music playing]

05:38.672 --> 05:40.215
[sighs]

05:40.299 --> 05:42.009
[stammering] Is it something else?

05:42.092 --> 05:43.635
Uh…

05:43.719 --> 05:47.347
Oh. Is it because
I came in after you to class this morning?

05:48.599 --> 05:50.142
Uh…

05:50.225 --> 05:51.393
If not…

05:51.477 --> 05:52.728
Look at that math nerd.

05:52.811 --> 05:54.104
Wow, he's so full of himself.

05:55.064 --> 05:58.692
[sighs] If you perhaps heard
what I said earlier, Mr. Ga,

05:58.776 --> 05:59.860
I wasn't thinking straight.

05:59.943 --> 06:02.696
And it's all because
of the cracked screen on my phone and…

06:05.574 --> 06:06.992
[sighs]

06:07.076 --> 06:08.869
I'm really sorry. I wasn't thinking.

06:08.952 --> 06:11.413
-I can't believe I said that.
-That's not it.

06:11.497 --> 06:13.248
How on earth did you get a four?

06:19.671 --> 06:20.964
Oh.

06:22.132 --> 06:23.133
I…

06:23.634 --> 06:26.637
I don't even want to open a math book.

06:27.387 --> 06:30.099
It's hard and boring.
I don't get the point of studying it.

06:30.641 --> 06:31.767
I don't like it.

06:33.060 --> 06:34.394
It's hard.

06:34.478 --> 06:35.521
And boring.

06:36.355 --> 06:38.607
-And you don't like it?
-Right.

06:40.484 --> 06:41.485
[sighs]

06:41.568 --> 06:42.569
What is math?

06:44.363 --> 06:45.906
Math is…

06:47.157 --> 06:48.158
Math is math.

06:48.742 --> 06:52.037
How can you be so sure that you hate math
when you don't even know what it is.

06:52.621 --> 06:55.249
Mathematics came from philosophy.
What's philosophy?

06:56.291 --> 06:57.918
It's about thinking accurately.

06:58.877 --> 07:00.212
Thinking.

07:00.295 --> 07:02.131
Have thought about why
mathematicians prove everything

07:02.214 --> 07:04.842
through logic? Why numbers are
the root of, all existence?

07:05.926 --> 07:08.137
-Nope.
-See? And you say you don't like it.

07:12.099 --> 07:14.601
You will write a letter to Euclid
reflecting on

07:14.685 --> 07:16.979
what you don't know,
and where math comes from.

07:17.980 --> 07:21.608
It has to be 20 pages long and ready
by day's end tomorrow.

07:22.484 --> 07:23.360
Twenty pages?

07:23.443 --> 07:24.695
Send Choi Ji-a in.

07:25.821 --> 07:26.947
Mr. Ga.

07:28.323 --> 07:29.741
-[comical music playing]
-[sighs]

07:31.368 --> 07:32.369
All right.

07:38.959 --> 07:39.960
[sighs]

07:46.091 --> 07:47.426
Thank you.

07:48.218 --> 07:49.428
What's your next class?

07:51.972 --> 07:52.973
[door opens]

07:53.640 --> 07:55.225
[students] Hello.

07:58.187 --> 08:01.690
Let me apologize on Mr. Ga's behalf
for this morning.

08:02.399 --> 08:04.818
He can be really cranky sometimes,
you see.

08:05.444 --> 08:07.779
[sighs] He's immature and childish
at times.

08:08.405 --> 08:09.990
But he is truly a good person at heart.

08:10.574 --> 08:13.076
[chuckles] Right.

08:13.160 --> 08:14.494
[Eui-ju] That's not it at all.

08:14.578 --> 08:16.747
He's totally messing with you.

08:16.830 --> 08:19.875
You really don't have to defend him
like that Mr. Yoon.

08:19.958 --> 08:21.793
Oh. Mr. Yoon, I…

08:21.877 --> 08:22.878
Oh. [chuckles]

08:22.961 --> 08:24.671
-[chuckles]
-It was nice seeing you today.

08:30.427 --> 08:31.720
[sighs]

08:31.803 --> 08:33.388
He's a total angel.

08:33.931 --> 08:34.932
[chuckles]

08:35.015 --> 08:37.434
How did he end up with a demon like him?

08:38.518 --> 08:39.353
[tuts]

08:39.937 --> 08:41.939
[footsteps approaching]

08:44.900 --> 08:45.901
Ji-a.

08:48.779 --> 08:49.905
Choi Ji-a!

08:51.114 --> 08:52.157
Hey, wake up.

08:53.075 --> 08:55.827
Come on and wake up.

08:59.206 --> 09:00.249
Mr. Ga's calling you.

09:01.458 --> 09:02.626
[sighs]

09:09.007 --> 09:10.801
-[door opens]
-So?

09:12.803 --> 09:14.513
He wants me to write a paper.

09:14.596 --> 09:15.806
Twenty pages.

09:15.889 --> 09:17.307
For what you said?

09:17.391 --> 09:18.684
No.

09:18.767 --> 09:20.644
Because I got a four in math.

09:26.608 --> 09:27.943
Why were you late?

09:28.026 --> 09:30.946
Did you sleep in? Or was there a reason
you didn't feel like coming?

09:35.075 --> 09:37.786
Coming to school on time
is also a promise. Don't you think?

09:43.208 --> 09:44.626
Please don't be late again.

09:44.710 --> 09:46.962
But if you happen to be late,
let me know why, okay?

09:47.546 --> 09:49.339
-Yes.
-Dismissed.

09:55.846 --> 09:57.180
[door closes]

09:57.264 --> 09:59.599
[sighs] That girl's in your class?

10:00.309 --> 10:01.852
With kids from shelters,

10:01.935 --> 10:04.730
all you can hope for is that
they stay out of trouble and graduate.

10:04.813 --> 10:07.107
Don't waste your energy trying
to lay down the law.

10:07.190 --> 10:08.400
And just keep it smooth and easy.

10:08.483 --> 10:10.569
That's gonna be for the best.

10:10.652 --> 10:11.820
For everyone really.

10:16.033 --> 10:17.367
CHAPTER 5:
YOU'RE SOFT AND SQUISHY

10:17.451 --> 10:20.996
"Our hall is a sanctuary of love,
steeped in ancient customs.

10:21.079 --> 10:24.875
Sun, close your crystal eyes like a doe.

10:24.958 --> 10:28.628
I shall comb my tangled hair like a lion.

10:28.712 --> 10:31.131
[Go-ya] From now on,
when I'm with you, Dong-ju,

10:31.214 --> 10:33.967
I'm going to be that girl
from way back when,

10:34.051 --> 10:36.261
-the one we all loved.
-[Dong-ju] "…leave us in the dark…"

10:36.887 --> 10:39.431
[screaming]

10:39.514 --> 10:41.058
[pop music playing]

10:41.141 --> 10:42.142
[exclaims]

10:44.519 --> 10:45.604
[grunts, groans]

10:45.687 --> 10:47.022
You need to place your hands a bit lower.

10:47.105 --> 10:48.357
Eui-ju!

10:48.940 --> 10:49.816
[student] You can do it!

10:50.400 --> 10:51.360
Sorry.

10:54.112 --> 10:55.447
-[students cheering]
-[gasps]

10:57.074 --> 10:57.991
Give her a hand!

10:58.075 --> 10:59.993
"I hope that we get along."

11:00.619 --> 11:02.287
-All right.
-[student] Mr. Noh!

11:02.371 --> 11:03.830
You look like Luciel of Else.

11:03.914 --> 11:06.917
[students chattering, chuckling]

11:07.918 --> 11:09.920
An agent picked me off the street
when I was younger.

11:11.171 --> 11:12.547
Didn't I tell you this story?

11:13.173 --> 11:16.802
-Tell us, Mr. Noh.
-Oh, please tell us, Mr. Noh! Please.

11:16.885 --> 11:18.428
So what happened was…

11:21.973 --> 11:22.974
It leads to this.

11:23.058 --> 11:25.185
Now, x minus y is not zero, right?

11:25.268 --> 11:27.229
And y minus z isn't zero either.

11:27.938 --> 11:28.939
Plug them in.

11:29.022 --> 11:31.733
[pop music continues]

11:31.817 --> 11:33.735
…2y plus…

11:35.612 --> 11:37.489
[scoffs] So annoying.

11:37.572 --> 11:39.783
[Woo-su] Since x is the maximum value…

11:41.660 --> 11:44.121
[music fades]

11:44.204 --> 11:46.039
[students chattering]

11:46.123 --> 11:47.124
[chattering stops]

11:47.207 --> 11:48.667
Good job today.

11:48.750 --> 11:50.877
[students] Thank you.

11:51.837 --> 11:53.004
Where's Choi Ji-a?

11:59.970 --> 12:03.557
She always skips the end of day and
goes straight home after the last class.

12:07.185 --> 12:09.521
Cleaning duties start
with Yeo Eui-ju and two others.

12:09.604 --> 12:11.731
Why? Cleaning duties start
from the first name--

12:11.815 --> 12:12.941
Dismissed.

12:13.024 --> 12:14.776
[students] Thank you.

12:14.860 --> 12:17.028
-[student] He's so cute.
-[chattering]

12:18.113 --> 12:20.449
[Eui-ju] Why did I have to tell him
what I said?

12:23.368 --> 12:25.954
[Dong-ju] Hey, it hurts. Be gentle. Ouch.

12:26.037 --> 12:27.998
[Gi-jeon] How nervous were you
to get this stiff?

12:28.081 --> 12:30.125
[synth-pop music playing]

12:35.714 --> 12:37.257
There.

12:37.340 --> 12:38.550
[Dong-ju groans]

12:39.134 --> 12:40.135
[groans]

12:40.218 --> 12:42.888
It nearly killed me
in the middle of writing on the board.

12:42.971 --> 12:45.015
-My arm suddenly felt so stiff.
-[Gi-jeon] Poor you.

12:46.349 --> 12:47.934
And your stomach? Feeling better?

12:48.018 --> 12:49.227
Yes.

12:49.311 --> 12:50.437
Oh, boy.

12:50.520 --> 12:51.688
How were your classes today?

12:51.771 --> 12:53.940
[Gi-jeon] Don't get me started.
I'm dying to go home.

12:54.024 --> 12:54.983
That feels good.

12:56.234 --> 12:57.486
No, the other arm is okay.

12:57.569 --> 12:59.029
-[Gi-jeon sighs]
-[gasps]

12:59.112 --> 13:00.280
[Gi-jeon] I'm just touching you

13:01.031 --> 13:02.616
because you're soft and squishy.

13:02.699 --> 13:03.909
[gasps]

13:04.409 --> 13:07.454
[Eui-ju] Oh. "You're soft and squishy"?
[gasps]

13:07.537 --> 13:10.248
Girls are more fearless than boys,
don't you think?

13:10.332 --> 13:11.625
My point exactly.

13:11.708 --> 13:15.170
They stared at me so much
that I didn't know where to look at all.

13:15.253 --> 13:16.505
And I ended up going blank.

13:17.088 --> 13:18.924
Ugh, I'm so embarrassed.

13:19.007 --> 13:20.675
The great Yoon Dong-ju,

13:20.759 --> 13:22.719
shivering in front of his students?

13:22.802 --> 13:24.679
Man, they'd be so shocked
if they heard this.

13:24.763 --> 13:25.847
[Dong-ju] Get off me.

13:26.348 --> 13:27.474
-[gasps]
-[Gi-jeon] Maybe I'll warn them.

13:27.557 --> 13:28.600
Oh, dang.

13:29.392 --> 13:31.478
Why didn't I come up with those lines?

13:32.020 --> 13:33.522
"You're soft and squishy."

13:34.147 --> 13:36.233
"Because you're soft and squishy."

13:37.192 --> 13:38.193
[chuckles]

13:39.152 --> 13:40.987
-[grunts]
-[Dong-ju] Mind your own business.

13:41.071 --> 13:42.280
[Gi-jeon laughing]

13:43.031 --> 13:44.199
Oh!

13:46.535 --> 13:47.786
[groans]

13:47.869 --> 13:50.455
You're so perverted, Yeo Eui-ju.

13:56.378 --> 13:57.837
-Hi.
-[friend] Oh, hey.

13:59.214 --> 14:00.632
Is it that bad?

14:00.715 --> 14:02.592
It's not that bad.
I'm sorry I asked so suddenly.

14:02.676 --> 14:03.552
No worries.

14:04.469 --> 14:06.179
Want to try this medicine?

14:06.263 --> 14:08.139
It's from my mom, it works quite well.

14:08.223 --> 14:09.766
[sighs] Thank you so much.

14:10.308 --> 14:12.102
I'll do the shift here on Thursday.

14:12.185 --> 14:13.770
It's all right. I can do it too.

14:13.853 --> 14:15.313
I have things to do anyway.

14:15.397 --> 14:16.773
Oh, I see.

14:16.856 --> 14:17.941
I'll be off, then.

14:18.024 --> 14:19.025
Bye.

14:26.491 --> 14:27.784
[laptop chimes]

14:32.914 --> 14:34.708
PAZER WEB NOVEL PORTAL
BEST WEB NOVEL RANKINGS

14:34.791 --> 14:36.042
[sighs]

14:36.126 --> 14:37.377
Lucky them.

14:38.169 --> 14:40.380
When will I get to be ranked this high?

14:40.463 --> 14:42.549
I WAKE UP AND FIND MYSELF
HIS SECRETARY

14:42.632 --> 14:46.052
"I woke up as secretary.
Came back as an evil slave?"

14:46.136 --> 14:48.388
Is the regression genre still trending?

14:48.471 --> 14:50.348
Ah… I tried something similar once.

14:50.432 --> 14:51.641
[sighs]

14:51.725 --> 14:53.810
But it was a total failure though.

14:54.394 --> 14:56.938
Should I just make it a sad story
with a tragic ending?

14:57.022 --> 14:59.399
Obsession and terminal illness?

14:59.482 --> 15:02.068
I've tried every scenario already. [sighs]

15:03.194 --> 15:04.529
[ping]

15:04.613 --> 15:06.656
-Or…
-[playful, pensive music playing]

15:06.740 --> 15:08.074
Because you're soft and squishy.

15:10.660 --> 15:11.911
Friends?

15:14.122 --> 15:16.916
What if they were friends from childhood?

15:18.376 --> 15:19.502
[character] I'm bored.

15:22.714 --> 15:25.884
I'm bored, I'm bored, I'm bored.

15:27.010 --> 15:28.094
You're annoying.

15:29.638 --> 15:30.972
Stop it.

15:31.056 --> 15:32.140
You're annoying.

15:32.223 --> 15:33.725
-[pen clatters]
-This pen is annoying.

15:36.019 --> 15:38.021
[playful, pensive music continues]

15:40.732 --> 15:42.942
[clears throat] No way. No way.

15:43.818 --> 15:45.945
They're my teachers.
I shouldn't drag them into this.

15:46.029 --> 15:47.739
[inhales deeply] No way.

15:47.822 --> 15:48.698
No, no, no.

15:48.782 --> 15:50.200
[student] This one please.

15:55.163 --> 15:56.456
[scanner beeps]

15:56.539 --> 15:57.666
Just a moment.

15:57.749 --> 16:01.378
CHAPTER 6:
MY FIRST SNOW… IS A BLIZZARD

16:01.461 --> 16:03.755
[rock music playing]

16:10.720 --> 16:12.722
[alarm blaring]

16:15.892 --> 16:18.812
Hey. Wake him up. It's too loud!

16:18.895 --> 16:20.563
That darn alarm of his…

16:20.647 --> 16:21.648
Wake him up.

16:22.273 --> 16:23.817
[grunts] Okay.

16:28.822 --> 16:30.615
[alarm continues blaring]

16:33.201 --> 16:35.370
-[Gi-jeon] What's wrong with him?
-[alarm stops]

16:35.453 --> 16:36.454
Da-ju!

16:37.205 --> 16:38.373
-Noh Da-ju!
-Huh?

16:39.207 --> 16:40.208
Wake up. Come on.

16:40.291 --> 16:42.043
[groans] Okay.

16:42.127 --> 16:43.920
-Come eat some toast while it's warm.
-Oh.

16:44.629 --> 16:45.630
Is it crispy?

16:45.714 --> 16:46.673
[Dong-ju] Hurry up!

16:48.550 --> 16:49.926
[Da-ju sighs]

16:51.177 --> 16:53.304
Your alarm is like a siren. Huh?

16:53.388 --> 16:54.514
Lower the volume.

16:54.597 --> 16:56.683
It's so loud, every morning.

16:57.934 --> 16:59.269
It's not crispy.

16:59.352 --> 17:01.855
It's not crispy enough,
it's got to be crispier.

17:01.938 --> 17:02.939
Gimme!

17:03.022 --> 17:05.275
Noise pollution every morning.

17:05.358 --> 17:06.693
Have you no respect?

17:06.776 --> 17:08.820
Respecting others is common sense.

17:10.238 --> 17:12.657
Am I not allowed to use my alarm
in my own house?

17:13.324 --> 17:14.784
Attention, tenants.

17:14.868 --> 17:18.288
You're making things very difficult for me
right now.

17:20.415 --> 17:22.333
[Da-ju] I deserve some more respect here.

17:23.460 --> 17:25.712
Isn't that why you have the biggest room
in the house?

17:25.795 --> 17:28.214
He calls us tenants whenever he's unhappy.

17:28.298 --> 17:30.008
That's cheap. Don't you see it?

17:30.091 --> 17:31.092
I'm off.

17:31.176 --> 17:33.094
Did you just call me cheap?

17:33.178 --> 17:34.304
-Finish it.
-Fine, then.

17:34.387 --> 17:36.931
You carpool with me every morning, right?
Pay for it then.

17:37.015 --> 17:40.268
What are you saying? Hey.
It's just cause my car is in the shop.

17:40.351 --> 17:42.395
Guys, we're leaving in ten minutes.
Eat fast.

17:42.479 --> 17:43.480
It's 30k.

17:43.563 --> 17:45.231
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

17:45.315 --> 17:50.737
What do the green mountain
and the sea signify in this poem?

17:50.820 --> 17:52.489
They're literally a mountain and a sea,

17:52.572 --> 17:54.532
but in this context,
they represent the speaker's utopia.

17:54.616 --> 17:55.784
CHARACTERS
KOREAN LITERATURE

17:56.451 --> 17:57.535
[Dong-ju] Now…

17:59.162 --> 18:01.080
SONG OF THE GREEN MOUNTAIN

18:01.164 --> 18:03.166
We also have the night

18:04.042 --> 18:06.127
in the fourth stanza
and the stone in the fifth.

18:06.211 --> 18:07.295
DEPENDENT

18:07.378 --> 18:09.214
[Eui-ju] A dependent personality,

18:09.297 --> 18:11.090
a bit of a pushover and doe-eyed.

18:11.174 --> 18:13.009
KOREAN LITERATURE
DEPENDENT, PUSHOVER, DOE-EYED

18:14.719 --> 18:17.347
[Dong-ju] These are common daily words,

18:17.430 --> 18:20.975
but each of them symbolizes
a different meaning in this poem.

18:21.059 --> 18:23.728
That's all for today. Good job.
Class dismissed.

18:23.812 --> 18:25.355
[students] Thank you.

18:25.438 --> 18:26.856
Learn from me, little girl.

18:29.359 --> 18:30.360
[student] Hello.

18:33.738 --> 18:34.948
Excuse me. Mr. Yoon!

18:36.199 --> 18:37.200
Yeah?

18:37.283 --> 18:39.619
Here, this is a chalk holder.

18:40.203 --> 18:41.913
You might get chalk on your hands
without one

18:41.996 --> 18:44.707
because our school still uses chalkboards.

18:45.333 --> 18:46.751
[chuckles]

18:49.420 --> 18:51.506
[gentle, romantic music playing]

19:00.306 --> 19:01.432
Thank you.

19:10.900 --> 19:11.901
Go-ya, right?

19:11.985 --> 19:13.695
[wind whistling]

19:13.778 --> 19:14.612
Huh?

19:15.780 --> 19:16.781
Thanks for this.

19:23.705 --> 19:24.706
Hey.

19:24.789 --> 19:26.457
[gentle music continues]

19:28.042 --> 19:30.003
What the… What's wrong?

19:31.296 --> 19:35.091
I'm up against a formidable opponent.

19:37.010 --> 19:38.052
He is a first snow

19:39.888 --> 19:40.889
and a blizzard.

19:47.061 --> 19:48.062
[music ends]

19:48.146 --> 19:50.189
[students chattering, giggling]

19:51.441 --> 19:53.401
[student] Rock, paper, scissors, shoot.

19:55.695 --> 19:56.738
Let's go again.

19:57.280 --> 20:00.366
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot.

20:02.827 --> 20:04.954
[rock music playing]

20:09.208 --> 20:10.960
[Eui-ju] Old-school tough guy.

20:11.044 --> 20:13.004
Strong. And he goes for it.

20:14.422 --> 20:18.426
Cold on the outside but a softie
for his guy, and kind of obsessive too?

20:20.178 --> 20:22.764
-Hi.
-[students] Hello.

20:22.847 --> 20:24.140
[Gi-jeon] Hello, everyone.

20:24.223 --> 20:26.643
Today, we'll be doing long-distance
running for your test.

20:26.726 --> 20:27.727
-[students groan]
-Not that.

20:27.810 --> 20:28.686
Five laps.

20:28.770 --> 20:29.854
-No way!
-Mr. Jung!

20:29.938 --> 20:31.689
The sooner you finish,
the sooner you'll rest…

20:31.773 --> 20:33.274
Line up in groups of 12.

20:33.358 --> 20:34.692
-Aw, man!
-[Gi-jeon] Okay!

20:34.776 --> 20:36.986
-[students cheering]
-[Gi-jeon] Ready!

20:40.490 --> 20:41.616
[inhales sharply]

20:43.326 --> 20:45.912
[pop music playing]

20:47.997 --> 20:50.124
-[whistle blows]
-[cheering]

21:00.969 --> 21:04.222
CRUSH THE CSAT

21:12.146 --> 21:13.356
[Gi-jeon] I'm just touching you.

21:15.566 --> 21:17.402
Because you're soft and squishy.

21:22.031 --> 21:24.534
What are you doing, Eui-ju?
Run, I know you can do it.

21:24.617 --> 21:26.285
Run faster! Faster!

21:26.369 --> 21:27.996
Go. Faster, faster!

21:28.079 --> 21:29.247
Go faster, go!

21:29.956 --> 21:30.999
Come on! Come on! Faster!

21:36.462 --> 21:37.463
Come on!

21:38.006 --> 21:39.424
[Gi-jeon, distorted] Come on! Faster!

21:39.507 --> 21:40.883
Faster! Come on.

21:40.967 --> 21:42.093
[exclaims]

21:42.927 --> 21:45.555
[pop music continues]

21:54.230 --> 21:58.568
[Eui-ju] Stop it, Eui-ju!
This is enough. Stop, stop, stop!

21:58.651 --> 22:00.528
[cheering]

22:06.159 --> 22:07.160
[Gi-jeon] That's it!

22:09.245 --> 22:11.414
[cheering]

22:26.262 --> 22:27.555
[whistle blows]

22:27.638 --> 22:30.516
[cheering]

22:30.600 --> 22:32.393
Whoever wins, I don't care!

22:32.477 --> 22:33.478
[sighs]

22:34.228 --> 22:36.022
-[Gi-jeon] Are you okay?
-[music ends]

22:37.648 --> 22:38.649
[Eui-ju clears throat]

22:40.359 --> 22:41.527
[distorted] You okay or what?

22:43.905 --> 22:45.782
Yes. I'm okay.

22:48.743 --> 22:50.161
[distorted] Were you an athlete?

22:52.455 --> 22:53.331
No.

22:53.414 --> 22:55.416
[comical music playing]

22:56.167 --> 22:57.794
Wanna try after-school PE?

22:58.377 --> 23:02.298
It's at 5:00 p.m and it's every Wednesday.
We focus on the fitness test.

23:02.381 --> 23:03.841
You should give it a try.

23:05.760 --> 23:07.011
[chuckles] Uh…

23:07.804 --> 23:09.138
You've got potential.

23:13.601 --> 23:17.396
[stammering] Mr. Jeon,
let me go wash my face. [chuckles]

23:19.273 --> 23:20.817
[cheering]

23:24.612 --> 23:26.364
[Gi-jeon] All right. Okay!

23:26.447 --> 23:28.449
[students cheering, chanting]

23:33.204 --> 23:34.539
[sighs]

23:34.622 --> 23:37.041
This is nuts. This is nuts.

23:37.125 --> 23:38.835
Why is my heart racing right now?

23:39.961 --> 23:41.087
No way.

23:42.338 --> 23:43.381
[Gi-jeon] You've got potential.

23:45.424 --> 23:46.509
It can't be.

23:46.592 --> 23:47.677
It can't be!

23:47.760 --> 23:50.805
My heart, races even for a hero
in a novel.

23:50.888 --> 23:52.181
Yeah. [sniffs]

23:52.265 --> 23:53.516
That's just it.

23:53.599 --> 23:55.017
[chuckles, inhales deeply]

23:55.101 --> 23:56.102
[sighs]

23:57.228 --> 24:01.065
CHAPTER 7:
WE WERE FRIENDS

24:01.149 --> 24:03.609
CHARACTERS - KOREAN LITERATURE:
DEPENDENT PERSONALITY

24:03.693 --> 24:06.195
PE: LOYAL AND DEPENDABLE TYPE

24:08.239 --> 24:10.575
[sighs deeply]

24:14.328 --> 24:17.832
[inhales sharply] There are no obstacles
between the two of them.

24:18.875 --> 24:21.878
I guess I do need a second lead
to shake things up.

24:21.961 --> 24:24.088
PE, KANG TAE-HA
KOREAN LITERATURE, CHOI YOON

24:24.172 --> 24:27.133
The foreign-educated Han Jae-min
as a second lead?

24:28.009 --> 24:29.010
Nah. That won't work.

24:29.093 --> 24:30.344
He's too shallow.

24:32.930 --> 24:34.348
[inhales sharply]

24:34.432 --> 24:37.435
[Dong-ju] He can be really cranky
sometimes, you see.

24:37.518 --> 24:40.021
He's immature and childish at times.

24:40.104 --> 24:42.231
But he is truly good at heart.

24:42.315 --> 24:43.858
You better not spread
what you filmed today

24:43.941 --> 24:46.903
or I'll teach you what it means
to regret doing something.

24:49.989 --> 24:51.073
Regretful?

24:54.118 --> 24:57.455
A guy who acts like a jerk,
then regrets it later?

24:57.538 --> 24:59.165
That's totally Math.

24:59.248 --> 25:03.336
An arrogant math genius
who turns down all those offers

25:03.419 --> 25:05.421
from Ivy League universities.

25:06.297 --> 25:07.798
But why would he that?

25:07.882 --> 25:10.509
To go to college with his friend
who studies Korean lit?

25:10.593 --> 25:13.512
[gasps] He acts like a jerk
but secretly he's in love.

25:13.596 --> 25:14.889
[exclaims]

25:14.972 --> 25:16.224
So, the story will go…

25:16.807 --> 25:20.519
Korean Lit has had a crush on Math
since childhood,

25:20.603 --> 25:22.897
always drawn to that bad boy charm.

25:22.980 --> 25:26.359
Meanwhile, PE watched him
from the sidelines, longing for him.

25:26.442 --> 25:28.903
Math didn't know Korean Lit's worth
and treated him badly

25:28.986 --> 25:31.322
only to realize his true feelings
far too late.

25:31.405 --> 25:32.490
[gasps]

25:32.573 --> 25:36.619
My goodness. He's so in denial that
he tries to avoid Korean Lit.

25:37.536 --> 25:40.414
But PE returns as a possessive guy,

25:40.498 --> 25:44.794
and Math clings to Korean Lit in tears
as a regretful guy.

25:47.338 --> 25:48.381
[sighs]

25:48.464 --> 25:51.592
This is insane. This chemistry is insane.

25:51.676 --> 25:52.551
This ship is…

25:53.219 --> 25:54.387
[sighs]

25:54.470 --> 25:55.513
…going to sail.

25:56.013 --> 25:57.056
[exclaims]

25:57.139 --> 25:59.141
WE WERE FRIENDS
EPISODE 1

25:59.225 --> 26:00.476
IMUK

26:00.559 --> 26:04.522
AS DAWN BEGAN TO BREAK…

26:05.690 --> 26:08.276
AS USUAL, CHOI YOON
WAS THE FIRST TO WAKE.

26:09.527 --> 26:12.029
SEEING YOON SOBBING,
TAE-HA CAN'T HOLD BACK.

26:12.113 --> 26:13.114
Are you an idiot?

26:13.906 --> 26:14.907
Huh?

26:17.576 --> 26:20.413
What do you even see in that prick
who treats you like trash?

26:21.831 --> 26:23.874
He can be cranky sometimes, you see.

26:24.834 --> 26:26.794
He's immature and childish at times

26:26.877 --> 26:28.462
but he's really good at heart.

26:29.964 --> 26:33.467
He's not mean to me on purpose,
so don't take it personally.

26:34.760 --> 26:36.304
HE'S JUST USING YOU

26:38.472 --> 26:40.099
That punk is just using you

26:41.183 --> 26:43.561
because he knows that
you have a kind heart.

26:47.231 --> 26:48.691
It doesn't matter.

26:50.234 --> 26:53.404
Still, you're the only one
who worries about me.

26:54.447 --> 26:56.324
You're indeed a good friend of mine.

26:58.284 --> 26:59.285
A friend?

27:00.119 --> 27:02.496
[chuckles] My very best friend.

27:02.580 --> 27:04.206
YOON'S EYES CRINKLE AS HE SMILES

27:04.290 --> 27:05.583
[Tae-ha] I feel angry.

27:05.666 --> 27:07.126
Your words sound like

27:07.710 --> 27:09.628
you're telling me to stay away.

27:15.926 --> 27:16.761
Ah.

27:18.971 --> 27:19.930
TAE-HA PUSHES YOON AWAY

27:20.014 --> 27:21.140
What about Ju Si-on?

27:22.683 --> 27:23.601
What is he to you?

27:23.684 --> 27:26.479
TAE-HA'S VOICE TREMBLED
WITH JEALOUSY AND FEAR

27:26.562 --> 27:27.563
Si-on is…

27:27.646 --> 27:28.564
CHOI YOON HESITATED

27:30.816 --> 27:31.901
[exhales sharply]

27:36.238 --> 27:37.239
What the heck?

27:37.823 --> 27:39.116
Why am I writing so well?

27:40.534 --> 27:43.621
[sighs] This is inappropriate.
I mean, they're my teachers.

27:44.455 --> 27:45.456
Actually.

27:45.956 --> 27:47.208
No way.

27:47.291 --> 27:48.501
I changed all the names in the novel.

27:48.584 --> 27:50.503
Nobody will catch on
to who they are, right?

27:50.586 --> 27:52.004
[breathes shakily]

27:52.713 --> 27:56.175
I've never had words flow out of me
so smoothly about characters before.

27:56.258 --> 27:58.469
[breathes heavily, sighs]

27:59.470 --> 28:01.180
Still, this is wrong, Eui-ju.

28:02.098 --> 28:04.225
What if you get caught later? I…

28:04.308 --> 28:08.020
SUBMIT A NEW PROJECT

28:08.771 --> 28:09.772
[sighs]

28:11.941 --> 28:13.651
[comical music playing]

28:13.734 --> 28:14.985
[strains]

28:17.571 --> 28:19.073
SUBMIT A NEW PROJECT

28:23.119 --> 28:24.453
[whimpers]

28:29.166 --> 28:30.960
[groans] This is too well-written.

28:32.461 --> 28:34.755
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 1

28:36.257 --> 28:37.716
SAVE DRAFT

28:37.800 --> 28:38.843
[Si-on] Hey, Yoon!

28:41.178 --> 28:42.763
[western music playing]

28:55.609 --> 28:56.610
What are you doing here?

28:57.611 --> 28:59.905
You ready to take
that Discrete Math lecture?

29:00.656 --> 29:02.116
[chuckles] Let's go.

29:14.253 --> 29:15.337
[mouthing words] Stay away!

29:27.892 --> 29:29.268
[sighs]

29:31.437 --> 29:33.731
[rock music playing]

29:42.031 --> 29:44.408
BEYOND EUI-JU'S IMAGINATION
TAE-HA, YOON AND THEN…

29:54.376 --> 29:55.586
Guys, let's go!

29:59.590 --> 30:01.175
[stammering] What are you doing?

30:01.258 --> 30:03.677
AND HAN JAE-MIN

30:03.761 --> 30:05.763
[rock music continues]
